@startuml lling-architecture
' How libgrammstein plugs into lling-llang. lling-llang hosts a LayerPipeline that
' carries an input lattice through spelling correction, an optional CFG filter, and
' language-model rescoring, emitting a reweighted output lattice. The
' LanguageModelLayer is defined against lling-llang's LanguageModel trait
' (score_sequence / score_continuation); libgrammstein's HybridLanguageModel —
' a Modified Kneser-Ney n-gram fused with FastText-style subword embeddings —
' is what implements that trait. Colour follows the correction-* family:
' liblevenshtein/statistical blue, lling-llang purple, libgrammstein green,
' trait seam + lattice artifacts slate.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/lling-architecture.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/integration/lling-llang/overview.md
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Architecture — libgrammstein is the language model behind an lling-llang LayerPipeline

rectangle "<color:#263238>**lling-llang**  (WFST framework)</color>" as llang #EDE7F6 {
  rectangle "<color:#263238>**LayerPipeline**</color>" as pipe #F3E5F5 {
    rectangle "Input Lattice" as lin #455A64
    rectangle "**SpellingCorrectionLayer**\nfuzzy-matching candidates" as spell #1565C0
    rectangle "**CfgFilterLayer**\ngrammar validation" as cfg #6A1B9A
    rectangle "**LanguageModelLayer**\nrescoring with the LM" as lmlayer #2E7D32 {
      rectangle "**LanguageModel**  (trait)\nscore_sequence()\nscore_continuation()" as lmtrait #37474F
    }
    rectangle "Output Lattice\n(reweighted)" as lout #455A64
  }
}

rectangle "<color:#263238>**libgrammstein**  (language-model library)</color>" as gram #E8F5E9 {
  rectangle "<color:#263238>**HybridLanguageModel**\n<color:#263238>n-gram ⊕ embedding</color>" as hybrid #F1F8E9 {
    rectangle "**NgramModel**\nModified Kneser-Ney" as ngram #1565C0
    rectangle "**SubwordEmbedding**\nFastText-style" as emb #2E7D32
  }
}

rectangle "**liblevenshtein**\nedit-distance automaton" as lev #546E7A

' the lattice's journey through the pipeline
lin --> spell
spell --> cfg
cfg --> lmlayer
lmlayer --> lout

' the two integration seams
lev --> spell : fuzzy candidates
hybrid ..> lmtrait : **implements**\nLanguageModel trait

legend top right
  | Colour | Concept |
  |<#1565C0> | statistical LM core / edit distance |
  |<#6A1B9A> | lling-llang WFST host |
  |<#2E7D32> | libgrammstein LM & embeddings |
  |<#37474F> | trait seam — the integration contract |
  |<#455A64> | lattice artifacts |
  |<#546E7A> | external crate |
endlegend
@enduml
